# VAULT/Memory is written on more than one machine at once: the desktop's
# agents append to daily logs, calendar-writes.md, and MEMORY.md all day while
# cloud sessions commit to the same files. When both sides touch the same lines,
# a normal merge stops with conflict markers - and on the unattended updater
# (apply_update.ps1) that means the machine stays stale until someone resolves
# it by hand, every 30 minutes. `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides' lines instead:
# for append-only logs that is exactly right, and for MEMORY.md a rare
# out-of-order bullet is a strikeable line, while a lost one is not. Nothing
# outside this folder gets it - code conflicts must still stop.
VAULT/Memory/**/*.md merge=union
